Apple is planning to redesign the appearance of the iPhone 18e's rear camera, according to new design information from <a href="https://www.engadget.com/2325828/new-leaks-reveal-the-iphone-18e-will-have-a-redesigned-camera-plateau/"><em>Engadget</em></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/ipad-pro-camera.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1079220" /><br/>
The publication says it has seen computer-aided design (CAD) files depicting a raised housing that groups the camera, flash, and microphone together. It measures approximately 28mm by 35mm. This would give the rear of the device a significantly different appearance from the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17e/">iPhone 17e</a>, whose flash and microphone sit separately from its protruding circular camera.<br/>
<br/>
While the new housing would occupy more space on the back of the device, the drawings reportedly still show only one rear camera. <em>Engadget</em> likens the arrangement to the M5 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a>'s camera module. The redesign could indicate that Apple plans to upgrade the camera in some way.<br/>
<br/>
Earlier rumors have largely focused on changes inside the iPhone 18e. The leaker known as "Fixed Focus Digital" said a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/04/iphone-18e-rumored-to-focus-on-chip-upgrade/">chip upgrade</a> was the only improvement they could confirm at the time. The device is expected to use Apple's A20 chip, moving from the &zwnj;iPhone 17e&zwnj;'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/3nm/">3nm</a> manufacturing process to 2nm for improved performance and efficiency. Analyst <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ming-chi-kuo/">Ming-Chi Kuo</a> has also pointed to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/26/iphone-18-9gb-ram/">9GB of RAM</a> for Apple's lower-end spring 2027 iPhones, up from 8GB.<br/>
<br/>
Leaker "Digital Chat Station" has predicted a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/27/iphone-18e-could-get-two-key-upgrades/">6.12-inch OLED display</a> with a 60Hz refresh rate and a single 48-megapixel rear camera, along with a potential front-facing camera upgrade. "Fixed Focus Digital" subsequently claimed that the iPhone 18e could instead gain a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/09/iphone-18e-bigger-display-and-battery/">larger 6.3-inch display</a> and share a 4,430mAh battery with the standard <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18/">iPhone 18</a>. The iPhone 18e is also rumored to adopt Apple's C2 modem, replacing the C1X in the current model.<br/>
<br/>
